Phase 4 — Validate every finding
For every potential vulnerability:
•	Assign a unique finding ID.
•	Record affected component and severity.
•	Record the evidence and reproduction conditions.
•	Identify the actual security impact.
•	Confirm whether the finding is real, a false positive, or unverified.
•	Identify the smallest safe correction.
•	Add a regression test where feasible.
Never label a finding as confirmed solely because a scanner printed a warning.
Phase 5 — Implement fixes
Fix the root cause, not merely the scanner message.
Examples:
•	Remove exposed secrets and rotate affected credentials.
•	Move privileged provider calls to the backend.
•	Fix authorization and access-control checks.
•	Correct unsafe database access.
•	Fix insecure Android component exposure.
•	Improve storage and transport security.
•	Update vulnerable dependencies when compatible.
•	Add validation, rate limiting, and safe error handling.
•	Remove accidental debug behavior from release builds.
